# custom_frontend step 7 (docs/CUSTOM_FRONTEND.md sections 0, 5.2): the game's own three
# options screens, opened from the menu's SETTINGS panel (srfrontend.aptasm GoSettings).
#
# HandleInput prepend: while the custom front end opened the screen and the game is in its
# front end, B / Esc / START go back to the menu (the game's own Back goes to CONTROL_ROOM
# or nowhere outside the pause menu). The pause menu's use of the same screens is untouched.
#
# ExitScreen append: capture the game's live options (after the game's own ExitScreen
# applied them) into _global.SRSettings and the host store (fscommand SR_SetSettings), in
# the front end AND in game - that is how pause-menu changes reach the menu next time.
movie SCRGAMEPLAYOPT
prepend-to function HandleInput in ScrGameplayOpt file=options_input_head.aptasm
append-to function ExitScreen in ScrGameplayOpt
.const TAG = 'ScrGameplayOpt '
.include 'options_exit_tail.aptasm'
end

